===Etymology 1===
{{ety|en|:inh|enm:nede<id:need>|id=noun|tree=1}}
From {{inh|en|enm|nede}}, a merger of two terms:
* {{inh|en|ang|nīed}} (West Saxon), {{m|ang|nēd}} (Mercian), {{m|ang|nēad|t=necessity, compulsion, want}}, from {{inh|en|gmw-pro|*naudi}}, from {{inh|en|gem-pro|*naudiz}}, from {{der|en|ine-pro|*neh₂w-|t=death}}.
* {{inh|en|ang|nēod|t=desire, longing}}, from {{inh|en|gmw-pro|*niudi|t=desire, eagerness}}, from {{der|en|ine-pro|*new-||to incline, tend, move, push, nod, wave}}.

